#### Iterative Training via Self-Bootstrapping.

We adopt an iterative training approach that progressively improves verification capabilities through multiple rounds of RL. Unlike prior work that alternates between rejection sampling, supervised fine-tuning (SFT), and RL (Xu et al., [2025](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2601.20221#bib.bib13 "Incentivizing agentic reasoning in llm judges via tool-integrated reinforcement learning")), our approach operates entirely through iterative RL, following the RL-Zero paradigm where the model reinforces its verification capabilities without requiring dense turn-level expert demonstrations for cold start.

